<title>USA: German welfare system must be reformed - Issing.</title>
<headline>German welfare system must be reformed - Issing.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German welfare system must be reformed, not simply because of the demands of European monetary union, but to allow Germany to be competitive, Bundesbank chief economist Otmar Issing said.</p>
<p>Issing said in answer to a question at a business forum in Washington, &quot;I am convinced that the German welfare system has no chance to survive anyway.&quot;</p>
<p>He added that change was already underway in this area, but said that some urgency was needed to resolve the issue.</p>
<p>--Janet Northcote, Washington Newsroom +1 202 898 8300</p>
